prompt:
hey, i'm putting together a little meal-planning note and i want some mediterranean dessert recipes from you. like full recipes, written the way you'd actually jot them down in a planning note, with realistic timings and serving sizes and ingredient counts that all line up sensibly.

let me think about how many recipes i want. i was leaning toward 3 to give myself options... but that's more than i'll actually make, so let's keep it tight, between 1 and 2 recipes.

now the fields per recipe. each one needs a name, a prep_time_minutes, a cook_time_minutes, servings, difficulty, calories_per_serving, then the ingredients list and the instructions list. oh, i was about to ask for a tags field too so i could sort by occasion, but no, leave that out, i don't want any extra keys floating around that aren't in the spec.

types and bounds: name is a string. prep_time_minutes is an integer 5 to 120. cook_time_minutes an integer 0 to 180. servings an integer 1 to 48. difficulty is a string and it has to be one of 'easy', 'medium', 'hard'. calories_per_serving an integer between 50 and 1500.

ingredients is a list of ingredient objects, 1-20 of them. each ingredient has a name (string, just the base ingredient name, no prep notes), a quantity which is a number between 0.25 and 5000, a unit which is a string from this set: 'mg', 'g', 'kg', 'oz', 'lb', 'ml', 'l', 'cl', 'dl', 'tsp', 'tbsp', 'fl_oz', 'cup', 'pt', 'qt', 'gal', 'drop', 'dash', 'pinch', 'smidgen', 'handful', 'splash', 'piece', 'whole', 'unit', 'part', 'small', 'clove', 'leaf', 'slice', 'stick', 'sheet', 'sprig', 'stalk', 'stem', 'head', 'bulb', 'pod', 'ear', 'kernel', 'strip', 'cube', 'wedge', 'fillet', 'can', 'jar', 'bottle', 'carton', 'box', 'bag', 'packet', 'sachet', 'tube', 'roll', 'block', 'bar', 'pack', 'package', 'bunch', 'bowl', 'loaf', 'sleeve', 'scoop', 'mm', 'cm', 'm', 'inch', 'to_taste', 'as_needed' — and an is_optional boolean.

instructions: i first figured maybe 6 steps would cover a simple dessert, but for these i'd rather have it spelled out, so make instructions exactly 8 instruction objects. each instruction object has step_number (integer, at least 1), instruction (string), duration_minutes (integer 0 to 180), and temperature_celsius (integer 0 to 260).

for the format — part of me wants json since it's easy to read, but my planning tool reads yaml, so go with yaml. and put it directly as a bare array at the top level, no wrapper key around it. wrap the whole thing in a code block and don't write anything outside it, just the data.

here's the schema it needs to match:

```
{
  "type": "array",
  "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "name": { "type": "string" },
      "prep_time_minutes": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 5, "maximum": 120 },
      "cook_time_minutes": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 180 },
      "servings": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 48 },
      "difficulty": { "type": "string", "enum": ["easy", "medium", "hard"] },
      "calories_per_serving": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 50, "maximum": 1500 },
      "ingredients": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "name": { "type": "string", "description": "Base ingredient name, not including preparation notes" },
            "quantity": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0.25, "maximum": 5000 },
            "unit": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": ["mg", "g", "kg", "oz", "lb", "ml", "l", "cl", "dl", "tsp", "tbsp", "fl_oz", "cup", "pt", "qt", "gal", "drop", "dash", "pinch", "smidgen", "handful", "splash", "piece", "whole", "unit", "part", "small", "clove", "leaf", "slice", "stick", "sheet", "sprig", "stalk", "stem", "head", "bulb", "pod", "ear", "kernel", "strip", "cube", "wedge", "fillet", "can", "jar", "bottle", "carton", "box", "bag", "packet", "sachet", "tube", "roll", "block", "bar", "pack", "package", "bunch", "bowl", "loaf", "sleeve", "scoop", "mm", "cm", "m", "inch", "to_taste", "as_needed"]
            },
            "is_optional": { "type": "boolean" }
          },
          "required": ["name", "quantity", "unit", "is_optional"]
        },
        "minItems": 1,
        "maxItems": 20
      },
      "instructions": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "step_number": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
            "instruction": { "type": "string" },
            "duration_minutes": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 180 },
            "temperature_celsius": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 260 }
          },
          "required": ["step_number", "instruction", "duration_minutes", "temperature_celsius"]
        },
        "minItems": 8,
        "maxItems": 8
      }
    },
    "required": ["name", "prep_time_minutes", "cook_time_minutes", "servings", "difficulty", "calories_per_serving", "ingredients", "instructions"]
  },
  "minItems": 1,
  "maxItems": 2
}
```

stick to exactly these fields, nothing unlisted, and yaml only in the code block please.
